You are the editor of run `{{run_id}}` (task file `tasks/$TEND_TASK_ID.yaml`, worktree $TEND_WORKTREE_PATH): the one task that changes the shared files. The judges' requests are in the rulings under `{{gate_dir}}/data/rulings/` (`requests`, each `{finding, file, what, why}`); your manifest, `{{tasks_dir}}/$TEND_TASK_ID.json`, lists the files you may change.

## Apply or decline each request
Check each request against the Lean (`informal/declarations.json`, the source under `{{library_src}}/`) and the text; apply it with the smallest change to the file it names, or decline it with the reason. A section file you change must be one a request names. A notion a statement leans on and the conventions do not fix is fixed in `informal/sections/00-conventions.tex`, with its link (`informal/STYLE.md`, "The conventions section"), and the statement stays as it is: the conventions grow so that the items do not. Decline a request that would lengthen a statement to define a term, to name a typeclass, universe or index binder, or to restate a hypothesis, and say so. **Never change `informal/items.json`**: a change to the table is a proposal, `findings/edit/items-proposal.json`, `{"task": "edit", "changes": [{"item", "field", "from", "to", "why"}]}`, which the maintainer applies by hand.

## Write `findings/edit/edit.json`
`{"task": "edit", "answers": [{"finding", "status", "reason"}]}`, one answer per finding that has requests, covering all of them: `status` `done` or `declined`.

## Check, commit, finish
Build the whole document, `{{build_command}} build/$TEND_TASK_ID`, then `{{check_command}} build/$TEND_TASK_ID --aux-only --strict --declarations {{gate_dir}}/declarations.json`, and `{{gate_command}} --findings findings/edit/edit.json`. Fix what they name, commit, set `status: complete` in your task file and commit it.

